swer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{99}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e4654e7e-0783-5c4b-a381-592a4804452d" :activity/id #uuid "e4654e7e-0783-5c4b-a381-592a4804452d" :activity/title "The Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050928 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-75809ab1-ca36-5e2b-a707-ec10935a2237" "step-3845ff3b-fd6a-5233-99ae-c7ac1028703e" "step-03e32401-df3c-5835-ab23-3c8cb7d34eca"] :activity/first-step "step-75809ab1-ca36-5e2b-a707-ec10935a2237" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-75809ab1-ca36-5e2b-a707-ec10935a2237" :step/id #uuid "75809ab1-ca36-5e2b-a707-ec10935a2237" :step/content "question-3cfa23a7-bca9-5408-b04d-471de7fe17c9" :step/next "step-3845ff3b-fd6a-5233-99ae-c7ac1028703e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3845ff3b-fd6a-5233-99ae-c7ac1028703e" :step/id #uuid "3845ff3b-fd6a-5233-99ae-c7ac1028703e" :step/content "question-76554d51-a4eb-517f-a2a7-3724b0e31c74" :step/next "step-03e32401-df3c-5835-ab23-3c8cb7d34eca" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-03e32401-df3c-5835-ab23-3c8cb7d34eca" :step/id #uuid "03e32401-df3c-5835-ab23-3c8cb7d34eca" :step/content "question-9776a674-b453-514c-8110-e6416b1678fc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133905 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b1f3a877-5233-5d11-bd7f-f8b8db99c5be" "question-7fc30a95-4823-5308-bc3d-c38eeb6c9b5d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1f3a877-5233-5d11-bd7f-f8b8db99c5be" :question/id #uuid "b1f3a877-5233-5d11-bd7f-f8b8db99c5be" :question/math-academy-id "q-139575" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $8$ | $11$ | $14$ | $20$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-1$** | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $8$ | $11$ | $14$ | $20$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3f983e4-f068-54e8-9c9e-8a106c8c9d76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3f983e4-f068-54e8-9c9e-8a106c8c9d76" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f983e4-f068-54e8-9c9e-8a106c8c9d76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-593ac918-30c0-55f9-9a45-8bca67e90e57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76e17d5a-5046-5304-9556-d61074ae42ff" "answer-593ac918-30c0-55f9-9a45-8bca67e90e57" "answer-0ee8c8a2-5158-57a0-ad6b-eab622688ddb" "answer-1b31021f-f26a-5c88-9e24-49dab0b11f94" "answer-b96491c1-3d2f-5012-a011-55c9cccc0e67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76e17d5a-5046-5304-9556-d61074ae42ff" :answer/id #uuid "76e17d5a-5046-5304-9556-d61074ae42ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 11 & 14 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-593ac918-30c0-55f9-9a45-8bca67e90e57" :answer/id #uuid "593ac918-30c0-55f9-9a45-8bca67e90e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ee8c8a2-5158-57a0-ad6b-eab622688ddb" :answer/id #uuid "0ee8c8a2-5158-57a0-ad6b-eab622688ddb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b31021f-f26a-5c88-9e24-49dab0b11f94" :answer/id #uuid "1b31021f-f26a-5c88-9e24-49dab0b11f94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b96491c1-3d2f-5012-a011-55c9cccc0e67" :answer/id #uuid "b96491c1-3d2f-5012-a011-55c9cccc0e67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7fc30a95-4823-5308-bc3d-c38eeb6c9b5d" :question/id #uuid "7fc30a95-4823-5308-bc3d-c38eeb6c9b5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-139576" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-15$** | **$-10$** | **$-5$** | **$0$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-15$** | **$-10$** | **$-5$** | **$0$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3086de9f-7992-5290-a78e-b92ab10911d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3086de9f-7992-5290-a78e-b92ab10911d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "3086de9f-7992-5290-a78e-b92ab10911d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8987fbb9-4e36-5a31-a1b1-46618db9cc66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74dde18c-c7c1-59de-833d-07f07f975058" "answer-8987fbb9-4e36-5a31-a1b1-46618db9cc66" "answer-5fda055d-c731-555a-bf72-502387bb59a3" "answer-f2120fda-c38d-5064-839f-093917dee005" "answer-0878219e-c2fd-51d0-8c0f-8887e9b9bcc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74dde18c-c7c1-59de-833d-07f07f975058" :answer/id #uuid "74dde18c-c7c1-59de-833d-07f07f975058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -6 \\\\ -10 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8987fbb9-4e36-5a31-a1b1-46618db9cc66" :answer/id #uuid "8987fbb9-4e36-5a31-a1b1-46618db9cc66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fda055d-c731-555a-bf72-502387bb59a3" :answer/id #uuid "5fda055d-c731-555a-bf72-502387bb59a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2120fda-c38d-5064-839f-093917dee005" :answer/id #uuid "f2120fda-c38d-5064-839f-093917dee005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -15 & -10 & -5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0878219e-c2fd-51d0-8c0f-8887e9b9bcc2" :answer/id #uuid "0878219e-c2fd-51d0-8c0f-8887e9b9bcc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -3 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133804 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-685118c5-b7fa-5fb3-b5f9-06f8a56c7a87"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-685118c5-b7fa-5fb3-b5f9-06f8a56c7a87" :question/id #uuid "685118c5-b7fa-5fb3-b5f9-06f8a56c7a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-139647" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{104}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{104}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3.5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=3.5+x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32652aaf-8a9a-5672-9fc6-21a88c374b1a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32652aaf-8a9a-5672-9fc6-21a88c374b1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "32652aaf-8a9a-5672-9fc6-21a88c374b1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d6194152-573b-5c08-a9b7-e672113befaa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19864df4-2d2b-59b7-8b29-57ccd76568d5" "answer-c73853c3-d2b8-5386-8f71-11b0dfc356a4" "answer-ca337b13-8de7-56cb-a6fd-dfe6db160da2" "answer-d6194152-573b-5c08-a9b7-e672113befaa" "answer-2ffa906f-87d9-5316-b4b0-5c81c75eda13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19864df4-2d2b-59b7-8b29-57ccd76568d5" :answer/id #uuid "19864df4-2d2b-59b7-8b29-57ccd76568d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3.5-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c73853c3-d2b8-5386-8f71-11b0dfc356a4" :answer/id #uuid "c73853c3-d2b8-5386-8f71-11b0dfc356a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1+3.5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca337b13-8de7-56cb-a6fd-dfe6db160da2" :answer/id #uuid "ca337b13-8de7-56cb-a6fd-dfe6db160da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-3.5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6194152-573b-5c08-a9b7-e672113befaa" :answer/id #uuid "d6194152-573b-5c08-a9b7-e672113befaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3.5+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ffa906f-87d9-5316-b4b0-5c81c75eda13" :answer/id #uuid "2ffa906f-87d9-5316-b4b0-5c81c75eda13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3.5-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188348 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" "question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" "question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" "question-f583a782-477b-5b0e-85b4-2269efa11788" "question-4e37507d-c5f2-5123-ae55-8166bf59d6ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188056 :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.352, \\quad 0.567, \\quad 0.801\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n![](images/2c/2c4ac4b0cf243ba8b49024132642a3856210daa5a603ed534e636caef0083629.svg)\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y \\sim U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a) = 0, F(b) = 1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a <            x <            b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX = F^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y = F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $1 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\lt y \\lt 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ y-2 & =-\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ 2-y & =\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y = 0.352,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.352} \\approx 1.214$\n\n- For $y = 0.567,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.567} \\approx 1.396$\n\n- For $y = 0.801,$ we get $x = \\dfrac{2}{2 - 0.801} \\approx 1.668$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188352 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-67a7dadb-337f-50e0-a564-1d8c6c18e0d9" "question-58d37898-ce2e-573d-a33c-7ebee5e8073b" "question-b352c39a-e73c-5f2e-8ba3-a028566bd47b" "question-3ef6d345-db21-5f3a-aad1-2b5e56cc5e56" "question-483ad5dd-d09b-5c15-bb9e-2524c193114e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188060 :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.354, \\quad 0.593, \\quad 0.792\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the PDF $f(x),$ given by\n![](images/ea/ea0ee4d1fcf2e423ebd438e784160e525cb2486e91ba833cd84aae9ff0568344.svg)\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y \\sim U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a) = 0, F(b) = 1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a <            x <            b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX = F^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nFirst, we must find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ corresponding to our random variable. Since our PDF $f(x)$ is non-negative only for $0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ we have\n![](images/53/535220c76d363aac546f42314de13394c1fd8b3001e95028a4215867ebc6ed41.svg)\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n![](images/8e/8eef1c7b3d8a69137cf7ac23ecf721751f43449d48b6f450256e15f501ee4c91.svg)\n\nNext, we need to find the inverse of $y = F(x).$ So, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ and $0 \\lt y \\lt 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y = 0.354,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.354) \\approx 0.362$\n\n- For $y = 0.593,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.593) \\approx 0.635$\n\n- For $y = 0.792,$ we get $x = \\arcsin(0.792) \\approx 0.914$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/id #uuid "be496a82-fb90-5b74-9be3-d9e0bf10ddb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-147598" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.112,\\,0.455,\\,0.800\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}, & \\,x\\le 0, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $x\\le 0$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{x} \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.112,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.112)≈-2.189$\n\n- For $y=0.455,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.455)≈-0.787$\n\n- For $y=0.800,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.800)≈-0.223$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e896c598-93c0-535b-bc5e-efc7006916d9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e896c598-93c0-535b-bc5e-efc7006916d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e896c598-93c0-535b-bc5e-efc7006916d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" "answer-e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" "answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" "answer-49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" "answer-30c8a159-2ab7-583f-b9ca-e09e33a5305f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" :answer/id #uuid "78ff442a-3704-51bf-96bc-0abf7085c311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.768,\\,-0.773,\\,-0.231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" :answer/id #uuid "e55cf5bc-1685-5922-8164-3a84b98c019b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.998,\\,-1.067,\\,-0.554" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer/id #uuid "8cde8170-c21d-53f8-bce9-7b3b74453420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.189,\\,-0.787,\\,-0.223" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" :answer/id #uuid "49f3228a-be25-54a2-b493-12bafe2ab3e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.657,\\,-2.134,\\,-2.002" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30c8a159-2ab7-583f-b9ca-e09e33a5305f" :answer/id #uuid "30c8a159-2ab7-583f-b9ca-e09e33a5305f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.095,\\,-2.423,\\,-1.956" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" :question/id #uuid "e9e69354-0b9b-54c9-b814-cf1944d62671" :question/math-academy-id "q-147659" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.257,\\,0.498,\\,0.632\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & \\,x<0, \\\\ {x}^{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1, & \\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0<y<1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.257,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.257}≈0.636$\n\n- For $y=0.498,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.498}≈0.793$\n\n- For $y=0.632,$ we get $x=\\sqrt[3]{0.632}≈0.858$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c6038e-d575-5102-98ac-e0a7869bfe80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" "answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" "answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" "answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" "answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" :answer/id #uuid "942bdd27-dcc3-5986-a885-d194ecacc967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.221,\\,0.467,\\,0.668" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" :answer/id #uuid "e39fbb91-ba93-50b2-be45-d43aa8372324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.281,\\,0.546,\\,0.771" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" :answer/id #uuid "8420c9eb-cfa9-54a2-86e8-b718c39b55a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.467,\\,0.623,\\,0.845" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" :answer/id #uuid "6ffc6693-7918-5b27-a0b4-e3a0783bca18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.502,\\,0.798,\\,0.904" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer/id #uuid "88f1ede4-d25a-58dc-a83e-6b6a90d5dafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.636,\\,0.793,\\,0.858" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/id #uuid "d55d9f6d-31b7-5824-bc8b-1fe8f38e31d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-147600" :question/problem "Suppose the following random sample was drawn from the uniform distribution $U[0,1].$ \n\n$$\n0.459,\\,0.714,\\,0.938\n$$\n\nUse these numbers to generate three random numbers that follow a probability distribution with the CDF $F(x),$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nRound your answers to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $Y∼U[0,1]$ be uniformly distributed. Suppose that the function $F(x)$ is a cumulative distribution function, where $F(a)=0,F(b)=1,$ and $F$ is strictly monotonic on $a<x<b.$ Then, the random variable $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX={F}^{-1}(Y)\n$$\n\nis a continuous random variable with the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\nSo, we need to find the inverse of $y=F(x).$ To do this, we solve for the following equation for $x,$ taking into account that $0\\le y\\le 1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{-x}} \\\\ 1+{e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ {e}^{-x} & =\\frac{1-y}{y} \\\\ -x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y}) \\\\ x & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-y}{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the numbers drawn from $U[0,1]$ into the above equation:\n\n- For $y=0.459,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.459}{0.459})≈-0.164$\n\n- For $y=0.714,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.714}{0.714})≈0.915$\n\n- For $y=0.938,$ we get $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-0.938}{0.938})≈2.717$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b52405c-a88b-5363-9895-3267fa25f577" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" "answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" "answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" "answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-8da0c88726c8" "answer-88e93c2b-5a1b-5de7-a0d7-7a2abc878221"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer/id #uuid "2b81fbca-a77f-5477-8743-e223ca70c61d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.164,\\,0.915,\\,2.717" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" :answer/id #uuid "d9721a66-9348-50b8-a97b-da234d7ecc8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.802,\\,-0.456,\\,1.034" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" :answer/id #uuid "c18dea57-6ee4-588f-8bb8-36b1138d9007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.203,\\,-1.754,\\,0.650" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-508e3d35-7d7b-5100-b5d1-