 :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4cfcd9be-e783-55b0-99ea-fba6321bdddf" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cfcd9be-e783-55b0-99ea-fba6321bdddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b91cf26b-c838-5e5d-aa06-fc66092081b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef4a2f03-57e0-5d1f-8907-f7f6963d369c" "answer-ff3d60c5-46d8-578c-bb51-151bc60afbf1" "answer-b91cf26b-c838-5e5d-aa06-fc66092081b3" "answer-d71d8ced-67cb-5b4f-bc7b-de4475da4fe8" "answer-c12b47a2-9d98-55dd-aa4e-1bd6ee49e769"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef4a2f03-57e0-5d1f-8907-f7f6963d369c" :answer/id #uuid "ef4a2f03-57e0-5d1f-8907-f7f6963d369c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/00/009bd2b9fe689cb44c0bb4bbf5ccc21b3c7bd347b3bfc112ea34a15d0fd58cd5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff3d60c5-46d8-578c-bb51-151bc60afbf1" :answer/id #uuid "ff3d60c5-46d8-578c-bb51-151bc60afbf1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1b/1b50a13e835d1c467cb596c8364dc6a15e406fa4568b5953836e3788624bb3b3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b91cf26b-c838-5e5d-aa06-fc66092081b3" :answer/id #uuid "b91cf26b-c838-5e5d-aa06-fc66092081b3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ab/ab7ae0789e9d434b24a6f00b77bde26514fac1a375fe406d567c6f8560661d36.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d71d8ced-67cb-5b4f-bc7b-de4475da4fe8" :answer/id #uuid "d71d8ced-67cb-5b4f-bc7b-de4475da4fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c2/c284d316ccc20ff2a3f790fe7573b0250a6b2430b778e3c8e0fe7081368e3106.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c12b47a2-9d98-55dd-aa4e-1bd6ee49e769" :answer/id #uuid "c12b47a2-9d98-55dd-aa4e-1bd6ee49e769" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ea/ea43acbcaa5eaf10fef44753863bafed13f64bc684f06fbd60268deee23800ea.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111163 :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x-1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's re-write the expression, as follows:\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{-x-1}=\\sqrt{-(x+1)}\n$$\n\nTo obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-(x+1)},$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/d0/d078ff010c5bb8a05bfe08bd6585ebb334bda324c69f7c8498bde38dbd8cd234.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-(x+1)}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2fcd6900faf5246202403591c333f30a04ad6d5f51894ab509c229234976fc5b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186108703 :answer-field/correct 17592186108706 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a8011cb-eb86-5ec9-8024-d1a5101b449a" :question/id #uuid "3a8011cb-eb86-5ec9-8024-d1a5101b449a" :question/math-academy-id "q-279985" :question/problem "![](images/06/062562ff86719e1ea820642d424ac93705eb56f3ec9f49adbd09108735d4e284.png)\n\nThe graph above is a result of the reflection and translation of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$ Identify the equation that generated the graph.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/30/30add2e841bb25faa97692ec22309482c9b18d8c55f878057978f0896f7420ea.png)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/0b/0bab48c1fe5e6d1a0d90b1aae3c8cd123327d1b2e18ca8101e056726b76de002.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $1$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}.$\n\n- Translate the result up by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}+4.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/57/572a818b9621f8cec26f815429ff6d6e2846686afa348c7ae5a767dbd42fd3f6.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0c113b2a-ad23-5780-9cce-e37da6147575"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0c113b2a-ad23-5780-9cce-e37da6147575" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c113b2a-ad23-5780-9cce-e37da6147575" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1f4b416f-f7e3-507c-938f-37652289351a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f4b416f-f7e3-507c-938f-37652289351a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f4b416f-f7e3-507c-938f-37652289351a" :answer/id #uuid "1f4b416f-f7e3-507c-938f-37652289351a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{1-x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2cdfaece-91e9-59d5-8fba-ab96089ab7a5" :question/id #uuid "2cdfaece-91e9-59d5-8fba-ab96089ab7a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-89802" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{1-x}-1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's re-write the expression, as follows:\n\n$$\ny=-\\sqrt{1-x}-1=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1\n$$\n\nTo get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1,$ we can do the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/85/854a720d691342b87a7f390176cdc60cf5d68d8863a755fed8929dbd3fecd655.png)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/b5/b5c145b598e3311edf3f9f6958245bd7a6b5a875e476d2f383e7c1c394f80538.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/7a/7a7c548b2d93636bb00902b62a37fd75fc7aceea00c71574d7761b46775eb844.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19b830fb-2397-5027-b124-14a89d3a6a96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19b830fb-2397-5027-b124-14a89d3a6a96" :answer-field/id #uuid "19b830fb-2397-5027-b124-14a89d3a6a96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ec96415f-9c0c-577f-9429-ab697ff9d175" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a605914d-130d-5995-b05e-d6ca34faf0a1" "answer-ec96415f-9c0c-577f-9429-ab697ff9d175" "answer-8545f868-355a-5980-bf30-3d293d470f6b" "answer-1e71492d-7e4b-506c-b7fb-5427c68ca906" "answer-c78771ee-cdbc-50e4-b2a2-d26c0253edf0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a605914d-130d-5995-b05e-d6ca34faf0a1" :answer/id #uuid "a605914d-130d-5995-b05e-d6ca34faf0a1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/15/159ea04f3e69844b91c8bb2b4739a27f604ed30f4fb1081fa0b7e95565ea6051.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec96415f-9c0c-577f-9429-ab697ff9d175" :answer/id #uuid "ec96415f-9c0c-577f-9429-ab697ff9d175" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/77/77eefc762f37b11fc65d942b5f6dd733ba60620f4a704936525bc3d69d6738e8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8545f868-355a-5980-bf30-3d293d470f6b" :answer/id #uuid "8545f868-355a-5980-bf30-3d293d470f6b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/be/be7b05a412acafde6ddb2c09e6df8731a078b46d38a8a722f57564043e40cd1f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e71492d-7e4b-506c-b7fb-5427c68ca906" :answer/id #uuid "1e71492d-7e4b-506c-b7fb-5427c68ca906" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ce/ceff2bebf692a1db8d0edb938543498d3930f29a1cc551f005bf8ac3b57f63d5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c78771ee-cdbc-50e4-b2a2-d26c0253edf0" :answer/id #uuid "c78771ee-cdbc-50e4-b2a2-d26c0253edf0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fe/fe3bed5784852da3bc18e4f277a1195a173b0168e08bb64f01c3c4f0641685aa.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111894 :tutorial/content "The graph of the square root function $y=\\sqrt{x}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/a4/a4d6f457f29cc6a292f23029967dc6fbb0c0f3905a04f34a430fddc8b211b0c3.png)\n\n  \n\nIn this lesson, we will learn how to apply graph transformations to the square root function. Let's start by considering translations." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111895 :tutorial/content "We can move the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ up or down by adding or subtracting a number. For example, to obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-3$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph **down** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-3.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b5eadb281202323377386e6b750a304ece8f39232d0c37dc5d4885004a6b588.png)\n\nSimilarly, we can also move the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ to the left or to the right by adding or subtracting a number to the variable $x$ under the square root. For instance,  to obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-3},$ we perform the following transformations:  \n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the **right** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-3}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d51b569648468c78445daa6b8dc658fe6e2e8cb24ca8308b60a1f40b07c7e29.png)\n\nRemember:\n\n- Shifting a function up/down/left/right does *not*  change the shape of a graph.\n\n- If $a$ is a positive number, then a transformation of the type $y=f(x\\pm a)$ is *counter-intuitive*: $f(x+a)$ moves the graph to the *left* by $a$ units, while $f(x-a)$ moves the graph to the *right* by $a$ units." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111896 :tutorial/content "We can reflect the graph of the square root function ![](images/35/35f3311d1bf6feffd9b0cdb6b4910ebf8111065bbec512558385afb246b30e0d.svg) in both the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) and ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axes.\n\nMultiplying ![](images/99/99daf2e095b0105b7aaf495a7c3d901cc574d0dc8dc7e67294fbced0edbaf920.svg) by ![](images/66/66ef4b5796888b4025ee2d8b3d516ec80741b341db9389696b6e77a4af5208d8.svg) reflects the curve in the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis. The graph of ![](images/10/103e3884f47f4bb0de41a1498e867b0523672c04de75345dbac027589882ae98.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eef724b522e133a2a537d1b6e1406bdbf17fe285ea43c278888ab4a4bc9fa58c.png)\n\nMultiplying the variable ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) by ![](images/66/66ef4b5796888b4025ee2d8b3d516ec80741b341db9389696b6e77a4af5208d8.svg) reflects the curve in the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis. The graph of ![](images/22/22049b72df0ed12fbbdc61eba867bc52a0786ea81fb6b26f35a2f82bcd1bc5b1.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/78/782eade24c5ab9e1af679f0a310fac2d3e20805d40ee97c695ea214ac71cf2f0.png)\n\nNote that ![](images/22/22049b72df0ed12fbbdc61eba867bc52a0786ea81fb6b26f35a2f82bcd1bc5b1.svg) is only defined for negative numbers and zero.\n\nNow, suppose we want to sketch the graph of ![](images/da/dac5078fc454b1978d14cbf61abe357b898c81885b4ed0274d469de53efaa1f3.svg)\n\nTo obtain the graph of ![](images/ef/ef1b3a5890e7db48752670eeaa86a7499678b614b78b767d4d3a8ed22fc55792.svg) we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of ![](images/98/981b16229c80f6cdc59aa58acdf4e0c05ecdb93cf05b5f4da61b2f7db0b03802.svg)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis to get the graph of ![](images/7c/7c760b28b0fcf32a1f8a2b63c8383d8bc0b667ef484b994478f0c157c36519f0.svg)\n\n![](images/b9/b95995b8ee5595d774f02d2c03c1170cc443b8f06f6ccbc634eeeb2aebe86357.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units to get the graph of ![](images/74/7458914f9f50a584f281fd213e9bd3ce60d33422fbbd6e679e411c342fd87d1a.svg)\n\n- Translate the result up by ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) units to get the graph of ![](images/da/dac5078fc454b1978d14cbf61abe357b898c81885b4ed0274d469de53efaa1f3.svg)\n\n![](images/26/263ea3a28314da17ba084bcb512976deb73483dfaa3ad149845c35634ae1d4a4.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110880 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186228238 :answer-field/choices 17592186228240] [:db/retract 17592186228238 :answer-field/choices 17592186228241] [:db/retract 17592186228238 :answer-field/choices 17592186228242] [:db/retract 17592186228238 :answer-field/choices 17592186228239] [:db/retract 17592186228234 :answer-field/choices 17592186228235] [:db/retract 17592186228234 :answer-field/choices 17592186228236] [:db/retract 17592186228234 :answer-field/choices 17592186228237] {:db/id 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6" "question-f491a1e5-e94d-5b1b-9331-94aa4176665c" "question-8e6e37b0-420c-5604-b7d4-9e71462bd5eb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6" :question/id #uuid "9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334828" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-174e2ccc-42c8-5609-b37a-59d23929885c" "answer-field-5604af13-50f7-5867-8a20-353ebbce0164"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-174e2ccc-42c8-5609-b37a-59d23929885c" :answer-field/id #uuid "174e2ccc-42c8-5609-b37a-59d23929885c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146" :answer-field/choices ["answer-646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146" :answer/id #uuid "646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "te^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5604af13-50f7-5867-8a20-353ebbce0164" :answer-field/id #uuid "5604af13-50f7-5867-8a20-353ebbce0164" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554" :answer/id #uuid "aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f491a1e5-e94d-5b1b-9331-94aa4176665c" :question/id #uuid "f491a1e5-e94d-5b1b-9331-94aa4176665c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334856" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17254fb8-737c-5411-ba14-63458b8c5c1e" "answer-field-adcf2066-3be2-5f5c-966d-7fbfbab80820"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17254fb8-737c-5411-ba14-63458b8c5c1e" :answer-field/id #uuid "17254fb8-737c-5411-ba14-63458b8c5c1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86" :answer/id #uuid "b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-adcf2066-3be2-5f5c-966d-7fbfbab80820" :answer-field/id #uuid "adcf2066-3be2-5f5c-966d-7fbfbab80820" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914" :answer/id #uuid "c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(t-s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229675 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228238 :answer-field/correct "answer-0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8271283e-49da-546a-bd56-2f6be5819b84" "answer-0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" "answer-b2307a16-a23b-5389-9b9e-da92d8558ad4" "answer-ccc40006-4513-51cc-b21e-641f0113825f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8271283e-49da-546a-bd56-2f6be5819b84" :answer/id #uuid "8271283e-49da-546a-bd56-2f6be5819b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" :answer/id #uuid "0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2307a16-a23b-5389-9b9e-da92d8558ad4" :answer/id #uuid "b2307a16-a23b-5389-9b9e-da92d8558ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccc40006-4513-51cc-b21e-641f0113825f" :answer/id #uuid "ccc40006-4513-51cc-b21e-641f0113825f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228234 :answer-field/correct "answer-7c469a0d-2752-523c-9d5e-eb188c66277c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e237bdb9-b23d-538d-8ede-1bde46c2390e" "answer-7c469a0d-2752-523c-9d5e-eb188c66277c" "answer-f34842c1-f721-52e9-9b77-d0abbbd36f97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e237bdb9-b23d-538d-8ede-1bde46c2390e" :answer/id #uuid "e237bdb9-b23d-538d-8ede-1bde46c2390e" :answer/type :answer.typ